alth checks with an 18% error rate. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all three regions with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 52675, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_014m59Aj9hCKyzg7myqkkPzU", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconcile_lookup", "reconciled_executed", "postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 52675, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_014m59Aj9hCKyzg7myqkkPzU", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 56699, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test build of v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. A fresh status check after the rollback shows all three regions on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone tries to deploy it again.\n\nNo approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_019YK3AjMmvR89NX9fAmaeih", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01M6UMBeNrW8UDEMcwDmzSVa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy production release is v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01F6ZAUobE7AeJBhW8b2X2E7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01VEn5TBdZFu5q2BVFhP9WK7", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BaPooGPPKZarPHx5qAgUog", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014m59Aj9hCKyzg7myqkkPzU", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks \u2014 rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "After deploying checkout-api v2.3.1 to production (us-east, us-west, eu-west), the service failed health checks with an 18% error rate. (The v2.3.1-rc build was also unhealthy in staging.) Rolled back all production regions to v2.3.0, the most recent release that was healthy in production. After the rollback, checkout-api is healthy on v2.3.0 in all three regions with a 0.2% error rate. Follow-up: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure before trying to deploy it again.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened the SEV2 incident.\n\n- **Cause:** v2.3.1 was live in us-east, us-west and eu-west, failing health checks with an 18% error rate. The test build of v2.3.1 had also been unhealthy in staging before it went to production.\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.0 was the most recent release that was healthy in production. A fresh status check after the rollback shows all three regions on v2.3.0 and healthy, with the error rate down to 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 (SEV2, checkout-api) is open and has paged the on-call engineer. It describes the failure, the rollback and the recovery. It also notes that the cause of the v2.3.1 failure needs to be found before anyone tries to deploy it again.\n\nNo approval was needed, because v2.3.0 had already been healthy in production.", "type": "text"}]}]}